{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And the man shall be clear of iniquity.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: when the man is clear of iniquity, the waters test his wife; when the man is not clear of iniquity, the waters do not test his wife. And this clearance is that he had not lain with her in any forbidden manner from the time he became jealous and she secluded herself." "<b>And there are those</b> who explained: if the husband has committed any forbidden act of intercourse all his days, the waters do not test his wife — and even if he lay with his betrothed in his father-in-law's house, which is forbidden by rabbinic decree, the waters do not test his wife, as it is said: ״ונקה האיש מעון והאשה ההיא תשא את עונה״ — when the man is clear of iniquity, his wife bears her iniquity. Therefore, if his wife were forbidden to him by prohibitive commandments or by affirmative commandments, even if he became jealous and she secluded herself, she does not drink, but goes out without a ketubah. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted in tractate Sotah: when adulterers multiplied, the waters of the sotah ceased, as it is said (Hosea 4:14): ״לא אפקוד על בנותיכם כי תזנינה ועל כלותיכם כי תנאפנה כי הם עם הזונות יפרדו ועם הקדשות יזבחו ועם לא יבין ילבט״ — that is, this great miracle, which was performed for them for the honor of Israel and because they are a holy people, and in order to cleanse them from mamzerut, will no longer be performed among them, because they are not clear of forbidden intercourse. This is ״כי הם עם הזונות יפרדו״ — that is, from the language of פרדה (mule), which does not produce fruit; so too they are steeped in Zenut like mules and horses, not in order to produce fruit but only to fulfill their lust. And ״עם לא יבין״ — this good thing, he casts away (ילבט) in his folly; and likewise (Proverbs 10:8): ״ואויל שפתים ילבט״, and in the Jerusalem Targum: וסכלא בשפוותיה מתאחד."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:29:54.306301712Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}